From 13ed24d66f1b7877b330cb067bc8614d3cb272a2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timothy J Fontaine <tjfontaine@atxconsulting.com>
Date: Sun, 17 May 2026 18:22:28 -0700
Subject: bifrost: profile-timer probe type and quantize key restructure
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

PROBE_TYPE_PROFILE_TIMER=10: new attach kind for the host-side
profile:::tick-Nms route.  load_prog_parse decodes a u64 period_ns
trailer; attach.rs's PROFILE_TIMER arm opens a per-CPU perf_event
(PERF_TYPE_SOFTWARE / PERF_COUNT_SW_CPU_CLOCK with sample_period =
period_ns), then attaches the BPF program via
perf_event_set_bpf_prog.  Bumps BIFROST_NUM_KPROBES so peer
LOAD_PROGs land in subsequent slots instead of overwriting.
bifrost.rs routes prog->type through bifrost_set_prog_type(
BPF_PROG_TYPE_PERF_EVENT=7) before the verifier so env->ops is
populated.  Slot tracks a perf_event handle; cleanup releases it
via perf_event_release_kernel.

AGG_KIND_QUANTIZE=7: quantize aggs now use PERCPU_ARRAY[1] with a
DTRACE_QUANTIZE_NBUCKETS * sizeof(u64) = 1016-byte value (the full
bucket array), rather than splitting per-bucket rows keyed on
bucket-id.  agg_snapshot.rs handles AGG_KIND_QUANTIZE by walking
the per-CPU array bucket-wise via a new
bifrost_map_lookup_quantize_buckets reducer in
kernel/bpf/syscall.c, then emits ONE row per (name, user-key)
with the full bucket array as the value.  For unkeyed
quantize (PERCPU_ARRAY[1] case) the wire k_size=0 so the host's
CrossTargetAggReducer keys it identically to FreeBSD's empty-key
quantize row — both kernels' contributions fold into one
cross-target histogram cell.

bindings_helper.h exposes perf_event_attr +
perf_event_create_kernel_counter + perf_event_set_bpf_prog +
perf_event_release_kernel for the bifrost driver, and the new
bifrost_map_lookup_quantize_buckets reducer.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
